{"seq":12,"trial_id":"v02-heldout-2026-10/openclaw-haiku-none-mu-v02-heldout/ms-06-phl-tickets/r2","wall_ts":"2026-10-26T02:05:21.320Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-14T09:00:00-05:00","args_digest":"ebbaa251f8df39caaf7577ba04b6f35ce758663f4417e80fd47e599ca0abeee6","actor":"assistant","via":"slack","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"C1253QW9NJ6","text":"@Bettina, here's the Coastal list for Pellucid Harbor Logistics (PHL) and Driftmoor Marine Freight (DMF). Pellow Home Living is left out as you asked.\n\n**Pellucid Harbor Logistics (PHL, Gulf Coast)**\n- Ticket #4419 (open): the `Yard_Dwell_Summary` report times out when filtered by container length. *(Moss, Coastal cheat sheet)*\n- Friction point, no ticket number given: chassis pool validation at Gate 4 during shift change. *(Moss, Coastal cheat sheet)*\n\n**Driftmoor Marine Freight (DMF, Puget Sound)**\n- Feature request #882: a bulk-clear button for departed barges, requested by warehouse managers. *(Moss, Coastal cheat sheet)*\n- Issue, no ticket number given: the tide-table import macro failed on Terminal B. Engineering gave the night dispatcher a manual CSV patch. *(Moss, Coastal cheat sheet)*\n- Request: a patched manifest CSV before the 06:00 shift. *(Moss, Coastal digest 2025-11-02)*\n\n**Needs checking**\n- Ticket #4419 is attributed to two accounts. The cheat sheet lists it under PHL. The 2025-11-02 digest says \"Kwame's port account logged ticket #4419 regarding barge slip 7 schedule sync\" under Puget Sound Operations, which reads as DMF. I haven't assigned it to either account. Kwame or support should confirm which account it belongs to.\n\n**Coverage limits**\n- No PHL or DMF tickets or feature requests appear in #coastal-team or #coastal-random. The channel items that mention tickets are for Pellow Home Living or Saltmarsh, so I left them out.\n- The share listing didn't show the `accounts/<account>/tickets` folders, so this list covers only the Coastal channels and Moss's Coastal notes